                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "236434640",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199409217639",
                            "num_reviews": 167,
                            "playtime_forever": 153,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 153,
                            "last_played": 1790638085
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As with the first game in this series, [b]Star Sky 2[/b] is a strange combination of a side-scrolling walking simulator with a choose-your-own-adventure game mechanic. This time out you may choose to walk as a young man (The Dreamer) or as a young woman (The Gardener) by walking off the right or the left edge of your screen.\n\n[b]Star Sky 2[/b] is a delight to look at and the animation is simple but charming. The music is enchanting. The rules of the game are easy to master. After that, you follow the same path over and over, triggering different combination of events until you exhaust all of the achievements. Some events on The Gardener's path will not happened unless some event on The Dreamer's path has been triggered, and vice-versa. The permutations get to be a bit much and the game became a frustrating grind fest towards the end for me.\n\nI purchased all three Star Sky games as a bundle so I cannot complain about value for money spent. I'm not sure I would recommend this game at full asking price.",
